    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0357" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2900 <hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >2/7</hi></note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chairman of the Commission of
                        Neutrals</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-06">February 6, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I telephoned Mr. Cohen this morning and told him that I was much gratified by the
                    news we had received regarding the results of the conference at Mendoza and
                    asked Mr. Cohen whether he would be good enough to express to Mr. Cruchaga my
                    appreciation of what has been accomplished. I told him to tell Mr. Cruchaga that
                    if we finally get the Chaco matter settled the credit will be largely his for
                    having succeeded in bringing Saavedra Lamas into line.</p>
                <closer><signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
